MAYOR OF BANDAR LAMPUNG

MAYOR OF BANDAR LAMPUNG

LAMPUNG PROVINCE

LOCAL REGULATION OF BANDAR LAMPUNG CITY

NUMBER: 03 OF 2019

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

MAYOR OF BANDAR LAMPUNG,

Considering : a. that in order to fulfill the constitutional rights of women, every citizen has the right to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity, has the right to obtain a sense of security and freedom from all forms of violence and to improve the quality of life of women which is one of the responsibilities of the Regional Government;

b. that in the effort to fulfill the rights of women, efforts need to be made by families, the community, and the Regional Government, as referred to in letter a, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Protection of Women;

In view of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 28 of 1959 concerning the Enactment of Emergency Law Number 4 of 1956 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1956 Number 55, Emergency Law Number 5 of 1956 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1956 Number 57) concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions Including Municipalities Within the Level I Region of South Sumatra as a Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1959 Number 73, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1821);

3. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of all forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);

4. Law Number 19 of 1999 concerning Ratification of ILO Convention Number 105 Concerning The Abolition Of Forced Labour (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 55, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3834);

5. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);

6. Law Number 13 of 2003 concerning Manpower (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 39, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia 4279);

7. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);

8. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635);

9. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);

10. Law Number 11 of 2008 concerning Information and Electronic Transactions (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2008 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4843);

11. Law Number 11 of 2009 concerning Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 12, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4967);

12. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);

13. Government Regulation Number 3 of 1982 concerning Change of Territorial Boundaries of the Municipality Level II Region of Tanjungkarang-Telukbetung (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1982 Number 6, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3213);

14. Government Regulation Number 24 of 1983 concerning Change of Name of the Municipality Level II Region of Tanjungkarang-Telukbetung to the Municipality Level II Region of Bandar Lampung (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1983 Number 30, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3254);

15. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence, (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);

16. Government Regulation Number 09 of 2008 Concerning Procedures and Mechanisms for Integrated Services for Witnesses/Victims of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (TPPO) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2008 Number 22, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4818 );

17. Government Regulation Number 39 of 2012 concerning the Implementation of Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2012 Number 68, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5294);

18. Regulation of the Minister of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for Implementation of Women's Protection (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2008 Number 2 of 2008;

19. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 15 of 2008 concerning General Guidelines for the Implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in the Regions, as amended by Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 67 of 2011 (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Number 67 of 2011);

20. Regulation of the Minister of State for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 01 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards (SPM) in the Field of Integrated Services for Women and Child Victims of Violence (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Number 01 of 2010);

21. Regulation of the Minister of State for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 19 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for Empowerment of Women Victims of Violence (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Number 19 of 2011);

22. Regulation of the Minister of Health of the Republic of Indonesia Number 61 of 2014 concerning Reproductive Health (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 169);

23. Regulation of the Minister of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 8 of 2016 concerning Results of Mapping of Government Affairs in the Field of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Number 8 of 2016);

24. Regulation of the Minister of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 04 of 2018 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment of Regional Technical Implementation Units for the Protection of Women and Children (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2018 Number 532):

With Mutual Approval of

THE REGIONAL PEOPLE'S REPRESENTATIVE COUNCIL OF BANDAR LAMPUNG CITY and

MAYOR OF BANDAR LAMPUNG

HAS DECIDED :

To enact : REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING PROTECTION OF WOMEN.

text:
Pasal 2

(1) Perlindungan perempuan berdasarkan asas: a. penghormatan dan perlindungan Hak Asasi Manusia;

b. keadilan dan kesetaraan gender;

c. non diskriminasi;

d. kepentingan terbaik bagi perempuan;

e. hak untuk hidup, kelangsungan hidup, dan perkembangan;

f. pemberdayaan;

g. kepastian hukum; dan

h. partisipasi.

(2) Perlindungan perempuan bertujuan untuk menjamin terpenuhinya hak agar dapat hidup, tumbuh, berkembang dan berpartisipasi secara optimal sesuai dengan harkat dan martabat kemanusiaan serta mendapat perlindungan dari kekerasan, diskriminasi, eksploitasi dan perdagangan orangdemi terwujudnya perempuan berkualitas dan sejahtera.

translated_text:
Article 2

(1) Protection of women is based on the principles of: a. respect and protection of Human Rights;

b. justice and gender equality;

c. non-discrimination;

d. best interests of women;

e. right to life, survival, and development;

f. empowerment;

g. legal certainty; and

h. participation.

(2) Protection of women aims to ensure the fulfillment of rights to be able to live, grow, develop and participate optimally in accordance with human dignity and honor and to receive protection from violence, discrimination, exploitation and trafficking in persons for the realization of quality and prosperous women.

text:
Pasal 4

Setiap Perempuan berhak:

a. untuk hidup serta mempertahankan hidup dan kehidupannya;
b. mendapatkan pendidikan dan memperoleh manfaat dari ilmu pengetahuan dan teknologi, seni dan budaya;
c. mendapatkan layanan kesehatan;
d. membentuk keluarga dalam ikatan perkawinan yang sah;
e. mengembangkan diri;
f. atas pengakuan, jaminan, perlindungan dan kepastian hukum yang adil serta perlakuan yang sama dihadapan hukum;
g. untuk bekerja serta mendapat imbalan dan perlakuan yang adil dalam hubungan kerja;
h. berserikat, berkumpul dan mengeluarkan pendapat;
i. untuk hidup tentram, aman, damai, bahagia, sejahtera, lahir dan batin;
j. mendapatkan jaminan sosial;
k. memeluk dan beribadat menurut agama dan kepercayaannya masing-masing;
l. perlindungan khusus dalam kondisi/keadaan darurat.

translated_text:
Article 4

Every Woman has the right:

a. to live and maintain her life and living;
b. to obtain education and benefit from science and technology, arts and culture;
c. to obtain health services;
d. to form a family in a legitimate marriage bond;
e. to develop herself;
f. to recognition, guarantee, protection and fair legal certainty and equal treatment before the law;
g. to work and receive fair remuneration and treatment in employment relations;
h. to associate, assemble and express opinions;
i. to live peacefully, safely, peacefully, happily, prosperously, physically and spiritually;
j. to obtain social security;
k. to embrace and worship according to her respective religion and belief;
l. special protection in emergency conditions/situations.

text:
Pasal 5

(1) Pencegahan dalam rangka perlindungan meliputi bidang pendidikan, infrastruktur, pelayanan publik dan tata ruang, pemerintahan dan tata kelola kelembagaan, ekonomi, ketenagakerjaan, sosial dan budaya;

(2) Upaya pencegahan sebagaimana dimaksud ayat (1) dilaksanakan melalui:

a. peningkatan kualitas hidup;
b. membentuk dan mengembangkan strategi dan kebijakanperlindungan; dan
c. membentuk dan mengembangkan kapasitas kelembagaan yang berkaitan dengan perlindungan perempuan.

translated_text:
Article 5

(1) Prevention in the framework of protection includes the fields of education, infrastructure, public services and spatial planning, governance and institutional governance, economy, employment, social and culture;

(2) Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are implemented through:

a. improvement of quality of life;
b. establishing and developing protection strategies and policies; and
c. establishing and developing institutional capacity related to women's protection.

text:
Pasal 6

Peningkatan kualitas hidup perempuan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 ayat (2) huruf a dapat dilakukan melalui :

a. memberikan akses kepada perempuan terhadap layanan pendidikan, kesehatan dan bidang strategis lainnya;
b. mendorong keterlibatan perempuan dalam berbagai kegiatan pembangunan;
c. memberikan pengetahuan, ketrampilan dan nilai karakter, budi pekerti dan ketahanan keluarga; d. mendorong program yang dapat meningkatkan kemandirian perempuan dalam berbagai bidang, baik hukum, politik, sosial, ekonomi, ketenagakerjaan, budaya serta bidang strategis lainnya.

translated_text:
Article 6

Improvement of women's quality of life as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (2) letter a can be carried out through:

a. providing access to women to education, health services and other strategic fields;
b. encouraging women's involvement in various development activities;
c. providing knowledge, skills and character values, morals and family resilience; d. encouraging programs that can increase women's independence in various fields, both legal, political, social, economic, employment, cultural and other strategic fields.

text:
Pasal 7

Dalam membentuk dan mengembangkan strategi dan kebijakan perlindungan terhadap perempuan, sebagaiman dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 ayat (2) huruf b dapat dilakukan melalui :

a. menyajikan materi komunikasi, informasi dan edukasi tentang pelindungan perempuan;
b. menyelenggarakan sosialisasi, advokasi dan kampanye sosial dalam rangka perlindungan perempuan baik kepada masyarakat maupun setiap unsur yang bertanggung jawab dalam rangka perlindungan terhadap perempuan;
c. menyelenggarakan kerjasama berkelanjutan dengan masyarakat dalam perlindungan perempuan;
d. penguatan dan pengembangan sistem data gender;
e. meningkatkan dan melibatkan peran serta dan partisipasi aktif masyarakat dalam perlindungan perempuan;

translated_text:
Article 7

In establishing and developing strategies and policies for the protection of women, as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (2) letter b can be carried out through:

a. presenting communication, information and education materials on women's protection;
b. conducting socialization, advocacy and social campaigns in the framework of women's protection both to the community and to every element responsible in the framework of protection of women;
c. conducting sustainable cooperation with the community in women's protection;
d. strengthening and developing gender data systems;
e. enhancing and involving the role and active participation of the community in women's protection;

text:
Pasal 8

(1) Dalam rangka membentuk dan mengembangkan kapasitas kelembagaan yang berkaitan dengan perlindungan perempuan, sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 ayat (2) huruf c dapat dilakukan melalui:

a. memperkuat mekanisme koordinasi dan jejaring kerja unit perlindungan perempuan;
b. Pemerintah Daerah membentuk gugus tugas yang beranggotakan wakil dari pemerintah daerah, penegak hukum, organisasi masyarakat, lembaga swadaya masyarakat, organisasi profesi, dan peneliti/akademisi;
c. peningkatan sumber daya pengelola melalui pendidikan dan pelatihan bagi aparatur penegak hukum, petugas medis, psikolog, psikiater, dan pendamping korban;
d. penguatan kapasitas kelembagaan Pengarusutamaan Gender;
e. mengoptimalkan unit layanan teknis;
f. menyediakan sarana dan prasarana yang memadai dalam rangka perlindungan perempuan
(2) Untuk melaksanakan ketentuan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) diatur lebih lanjut dengan Peraturan Walikota.

translated_text:
Article 8

(1) In order to establish and develop institutional capacity related to women's protection, as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (2) letter c can be carried out through:

a. strengthening coordination mechanisms and work networks of women's protection units;
b. Regional Government establishes a task force consisting of representatives from regional government, law enforcement, community organizations, non-governmental organizations, professional organizations, and researchers/academics;
c. increasing managerial resources through education and training for law enforcement apparatus, medical officers, psychologists, psychiatrists, and victim assistants;
d. strengthening institutional capacity for Gender Mainstreaming;
e. optimizing technical service units;
f. providing adequate facilities and infrastructure in the framework of women's protection
(2) To implement the provisions as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be further regulated by Mayor Regulation.

text:
Pasal 9

Bentuk kekerasan terhadap perempuan berupa:

a. kekerasan fisikdisebabkan karena perbuatan yang mengakibatkan rasa sakit, cedera, luka atau cacat pada tubuh seseorang, gugurnya kandungan, pingsan dan/atau menyebabkan kematian;
b. kekerasan psikisdisebabkan karena perbuatan yang mengakibatkan ketakutan, hilangnya rasa percaya diri, hilangnya kemampuan untuk bertindak, rasa tidak berdaya dan/atau penderitaan psikis berat pada seseorang;
c. kekerasan seksual disebabkan karena:
1. pelecehan seksual;
2. eksploitasi seksual;
3. pemaksaan kontrasepsi;
4. pemaksaan aborsi;
5. perkosaan;
6. pemaksaan perkawinan;
7. pemaksaan pelacuran;
8. perbudakan seksual;
9. penyiksaan seksual;
10. penelantaran.
d. Penelantaran disebabkan karena:
1. perbuatan yang mengakibatkan tidak terpenuhinya kebutuhan perempuan secara wajar, baik fisik, mental, spiritual maupun sosial;
2. perbuatan yang menelantarkan orang dalam lingkup rumah tangganya, padahal menurut hukum yang berlaku baginya atau karena persetujuan atau perjanjian ia wajib memberikan penghidupan, perawatan, atau pemeliharaan kepada orang tersebut; dan/atau
3. perbuatan yang mengakibatkan ketergantungan ekonomi dengan cara membatasi dan/atau melarang perempuan untuk bekerja secara layak di dalam atau di luar rumah.
e. Eksploitasi disebabkan karena:
1. perbuatan yang mengeksploitasi ekonomi atau seksual dengan maksud untuk menguntungkan diri sendiri atau orang lain;
2. perbuatan yang dengan atau tanpa persetujuan korban yang meliputi tapi tidak terbatas pada pelacuran, kerja atau pelayanan paksa, perbudakan atau praktek serupa, penindasan, pemerasan, pemanfaatan fisik, seksual, organ reproduksi, atau secara melawan hukum memindahkan atau mentransplantasi organ dan/atau jaringan tubuh atau memanfaatkan tenaga atau kemampuan seseorang oleh pihak lain untuk mendapatkan keuntungan baik materiil maupun immateriil; dan/atau
3. segala bentuk pemanfaatan organ tubuh seksual atau organ tubuh lain dari korban untuk mendapatkan keuntungan, dan/atau tidak terbatas pada semua kegiatan pelacuran dan pencabulan

translated_text:
Article 9

Forms of violence against women include:

a. physical violence caused by acts resulting in pain, injury, wounds or disability to a person's body, miscarriage, unconsciousness and/or causing death;
b. psychological violence caused by acts resulting in fear, loss of self-confidence, loss of ability to act, feelings of helplessness and/or severe psychological suffering to a person;
c. sexual violence caused by:
1. sexual harassment;
2. sexual exploitation;
3. forced contraception;
4. forced abortion;
5. rape;
6. forced marriage;
7. forced prostitution;
8. sexual slavery;
9. sexual torture;
10. abandonment.
d. Abandonment caused by:
1. acts resulting in the unfulfillment of women's needs properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social;
2. acts that abandon persons within the household scope, whereas according to the law applicable to them or due to agreement or contract they are obliged to provide livelihood, care, or maintenance to such person; and/or
3. acts resulting in economic dependence by restricting and/or prohibiting women from working properly inside or outside the home.
e. Exploitation caused by:
1. acts that exploit economically or sexually with the intention of benefiting oneself or others;
2. acts with or without the victim's consent which include but are not limited to prostitution, forced labor or services, slavery or similar practices, oppression, extortion, utilization of physical, sexual, reproductive organs, or unlawfully transferring or transplanting organs and/or body tissues or utilizing the labor or ability of someone by another party to obtain benefits both material and immaterial; and/or
3. all forms of utilization of sexual organs or other body organs of the victim to obtain benefits, and/or not limited to all prostitution and indecency activities

text:
Pasal 10

Setiap korban berhakmendapatkan :

a. perlindungan dari pihak keluarga, kepolisian, kejaksaan, pengadilan, advokat, lembaga sosial, atau pihak lainnya baik sementara maupun berdasarkan penetapan perintah perlindungan dari pengadilan;
b. pelayanan kesehatan sesuai dengan kebutuhan medis;
c. penanganan secara khusus berkaitan dengan kerahasiaan korban;
d. pendampingan oleh pekerja sosial dan bantuan hukum pada setiap tingkat proses pemeriksaan sesuai dengan ketentuan peraturan perundang- undangan; dan
e. pelayanan bimbingan rohani.

translated_text:
Article 10

Every victim has the right to receive:

a. protection from family, police, prosecution, courts, advocates, social institutions, or other parties either temporarily or based on a protection order from the court;
b. health services in accordance with medical needs;
c. special handling related to victim confidentiality;
d. accompaniment by social workers and legal assistance at every level of the examination process in accordance with statutory provisions; and
e. spiritual guidance services.

text:
Pasal 11

(1) Penanganan pengaduan merupakan serangkaian tindakan yang dilakukan oleh penyelenggara layanan terpadu untuk menindaklanjuti laporan adanya tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan yang diajukan korban, keluarga atau masyarakat.

(2) Pelayanan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) berupa :

a. melakukan wawancara dan observasi keadaan korban;
b. membuat rekomendasi layanan lanjutan; c. melakukan koordinasi dan rujukan ke layanan lanjutan dan pihak terkait;
d. melakukan administrasi proses pengaduan.

translated_text:
Article 11

(1) Handling of complaints is a series of actions carried out by integrated service providers to follow up on reports of acts of violence against women submitted by victims, families or the community.

(2) Services as referred to in paragraph (1) are in the form of:

a. conducting interviews and observations of the victim's condition;
b. making recommendations for follow-up services; c. coordinating and referring to follow-up services and related parties;
d. administering the complaint process.

text:
Pasal 12

(1) Pelayanan kesehatan merupakan upaya yang meliputi aspek promotif, preventif, kuratif dan rehabilitatif.

(2) Pelayanan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) berupa:

a. melakukan pemeriksaan;
b. pengobatan;
c. perawatan lanjutan terhadap korban;
d. melakukan koordinasi pelaksanaan rehabilitasi kesehatan dan layanan kesehatan reproduksi;
e. melakukan pemeriksaan mediko-legal meliputi pengumpulan barang bukti pada korban dan pembuatan visum et repertum.
f. melakukan pemeriksaan penunjang dan laboratorium terhadap barang bukti.
g. melakukan konsultasi kepada dokter ahli atau melakukan rujukan.
h. membuat laporan kasus.

translated_text:
Article 12

(1) Health services are efforts that include promotive, preventive, curative and rehabilitative aspects.

(2) Services as referred to in paragraph (1) are in the form of:

a. conducting examinations;
b. treatment;
c. follow-up care for victims;
d. coordinating the implementation of health rehabilitation and reproductive health services;
e. conducting medico-legal examinations including collection of evidence from victims and preparation of visum et repertum.
f. conducting supporting examinations and laboratory tests on evidence.
g. conducting consultations with specialist doctors or making referrals.
h. preparing case reports.

text:
Pasal 18

Penyelenggaraan pemberdayaan perempuan di bidang ekonomi sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 17 ayat (2) dilaksanakan dengan:

a. memberikan pengetahuan, keterampilan dan pelatihan kerja;
b. memfasilitasi pembentukan kelompok usaha ekonomi produktif;
c. memfasilitasi penguatan dan pengembangan kelompok usaha ekonomi produktif;
d. memfasilitasi dan bantuan permodalan; dan e. memfasilitasi pengembangan jaringan pemasaran.

translated_text:
Article 18

The implementation of women's empowerment in the economic field as referred to in Article 17 paragraph (2) is carried out by:

a. providing knowledge, skills and job training;
b. facilitating the formation of productive economic business groups;
c. facilitating the strengthening and development of productive economic business groups;
d. facilitating and providing capital assistance; and e. facilitating the development of marketing networks.

text:
Pasal 20

Penyelenggaraan pemberdayaan perempuan di bidang politik sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 17 ayat (2) meliputi :

a. pelibatan perempuan dalam pengambilan keputusan di berbagai level;
b. pemberian kesempatan bagi perempuan untuk menduduki jabatan publik;
c. partisipasi dalam pemilihan umum; dan d. pengembangan diri melalui organisasi untuk berserikat, berkumpul dan mengeluarkan pendapat.

translated_text:
Article 20

The implementation of women's empowerment in the political field as referred to in Article 17 paragraph (2) includes:

a. involvement of women in decision-making at various levels;
b. providing opportunities for women to hold public office;
c. participation in general elections; and d. self-development through organizations to associate, assemble and express opinions.

text:
Pasal 22

(1) Pemerintah Daerah berkewajiban dan bertanggung jawab:

a. membuat kebijakan yang memperhatikan kepentingan bagi perempuan terutama dalam hal pemenuhan dan perlindungan haknya;
b. memfasilitasi usaha penyelenggaraan pelayanan pemenuhan hak serta memberikan dukungan sarana dan prasarana dalam penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan;
c. menjamin perlindungan, pemeliharaan, dan kesejahteraan perempuan dengan memperhatikan hak dan kewajiban perempuan;
d. mengawasi penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan;
e. melakukan koordinasi lintas lembaga pemerintah maupun dengan masyarakat dan Dunia Usaha;
f. melakukan pendataan dan inventarisasi data perempuan;
g. menyediakan rumah aman.
(2) Pemerintah Daerah berwenang:
a. menyusun pedoman operasional standar pelayanan minimal bagi usaha pemenuhan hak dan perlindungan bagi perempuan;
b. melaksanakan pelayanan pemenuhan hak dan perlindungan terhadap perempuan;
c. melakukan pengawasan terhadap usaha pemenuhan hak perempuan dan pelayanan perlindungan perempuan; dan
d. mengembangkan jejaring kerjasama antar lembaga pemerintah maupun dengan Perguruan Tinggi, masyarakat dan Dunia Usaha.

translated_text:
Article 22

(1) The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility to:

a. make policies that take into account the interests of women, especially with regard to the fulfillment and protection of their rights;
b. facilitate efforts to organize services for the fulfillment of rights and provide support for facilities and infrastructure in organizing women's protection;
c. guarantee the protection, maintenance, and welfare of women by taking into account women's rights and obligations;
d. supervise the organization of women's protection;
e. conduct cross-institutional coordination between government agencies as well as with the community and the Business World;
f. conduct data collection and inventory of women's data;
g. provide safe houses.
(2) The Regional Government has the authority to:
a. prepare operational guidelines for minimum service standards for efforts to fulfill rights and protection for women;
b. implement services for the fulfillment of rights and protection of women;
c. conduct supervision of efforts to fulfill women's rights and women's protection services; and
d. develop cooperation networks between government agencies as well as with Universities, the community and the Business World.
